@cjw296 Thanks a lot for that!

> What I'd suggest is making `xlrd` the default engine for `.xls` files and `openpyxl` the default for `.xlsx` files.

I think that's exactly what we ended up doing in https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/pull/35029. Explicitly specifying `engine="xlrd"` for anything else than xls files is deprecated, and when reading xlsx files we now default to openpyxl (if it is installed, at least. If only xlrd is installed, we also raise a deprecation warning that people should install openpyxl instead)
